# The DockNeighbor OS hub-lite image: the router runs the hub-lite. The profile is the role; each board it runs on
# is in boards/<device>/ (its upstream pins, board name, partition size, channel and extra packages). One version
# for every board: a release tag builds and publishes them all.
DN_OS_VERSION=0.1.5
# On top of the device defaults, on every board. No LuCI: the apps are the interface. dn-status: the read-only status
# page on :80 (owner ruling 2026-10-05: radios, hub, cloud; anyone on the LAN; up with local administration off).
# relayd: bridge mode over a Wi-Fi uplink (dn-net mode-set {"mode":"bridge","via":"wifi"}).
PACKAGES="brvg-hub-lite dn-handoff dn-os-upgrade dn-hub-lite-os dn-net dn-status relayd -luci"
# The hub-lite (port 8722) and dn-status (port 80) each run their OWN uhttpd instance. The system one stays off: it
# would only serve an empty /www, and on :80.
DISABLED_SERVICES="uhttpd"
# The overlay (jffs2, bytes usable above its reserve) every board's image must leave free, checked on the built image
# by scripts/check-hub-lite-image.sh. It is sized for the hub hub-lite becomes, the Rust daemon's lite profile (R59):
# about 3.93 MB for one binary, a figure the Hub has not yet published per board. Room for TWO copies, because a level-1
# upgrade can hold the old and the new binary at once. jffs2's compression is not counted, so this errs high. Plus
# 256 KiB for the hub's own state and the dn-* packages' level-1 upgrades.
# 2 x 3930000 + 262144 = 8122144. Raise it when the daemon's measured lite build is larger.
OVERLAY_MIN=8122144
